1
00:00:03,250 --> 00:00:04,480
(Episode 81)

2
00:00:31,171 --> 00:00:32,181
Father.

3
00:00:40,681 --> 00:00:42,021
Father, you're sitting in the dark.

4
00:00:42,891 --> 00:00:45,461
Father, were you looking at your high school yearbook?

5
00:00:45,621 --> 00:00:49,031
- Yes, I couldn't sleep. - I see.

6
00:00:49,091 --> 00:00:50,091
Why are you still up?

7
00:00:50,161 --> 00:00:52,431
Eun Ae and I were about to go for a walk around the neighbourhood.

8
00:00:53,631 --> 00:00:54,831
Would you like to come with us, Father?

9
00:00:55,471 --> 00:00:56,701
No. I should get to sleep.

10
00:00:57,601 --> 00:00:58,631
I'll head down now.

11
00:00:59,201 --> 00:01:00,671
Yes, sleep well.

12
00:01:05,881 --> 00:01:07,941
- Shall we go? - Yes.

13
00:01:16,921 --> 00:01:18,251
Why are you still up?

14
00:01:18,861 --> 00:01:21,921
What? I should go to sleep.

15
00:01:22,861 --> 00:01:24,291
What is it? Is something bothering you?

16
00:01:25,701 --> 00:01:28,231
Me? Bothering me? No, nothing like that.

17
00:01:28,361 --> 00:01:31,101
You've been a bit off since dinner.

18
00:01:31,871 --> 00:01:34,301
The kids went to all that trouble to make us dinner,

19
00:01:34,571 --> 00:01:36,241
but you barely touched your meat.

20
00:01:36,541 --> 00:01:40,081
I did? No. I ate well. It was delicious.

21
00:01:40,341 --> 00:01:41,481
Is it because Eun Ae said...

22
00:01:41,481 --> 00:01:43,351
she wanted to follow Team Leader Ko to the US?

23
00:01:43,881 --> 00:01:46,321
- Are you upset about it? - Why would I be upset?

24
00:01:46,621 --> 00:01:47,621
Go to sleep.

25
00:01:48,081 --> 00:01:49,451
You get to sleep too.

26
00:01:49,721 --> 00:01:50,721
All right, I will.

27
00:01:51,951 --> 00:01:53,761
Oh, dear.

28
00:02:03,571 --> 00:02:05,171
I didn't care if anyone else knew,

29
00:02:06,571 --> 00:02:08,071
but I never wanted my kids to know.

30
00:02:10,271 --> 00:02:11,711
Not my own children.

31
00:02:14,381 --> 00:02:16,551
My daughter's whole world has been shattered.

32
00:02:19,051 --> 00:02:21,221
Team Leader Ko will find out soon enough...

33
00:02:24,091 --> 00:02:25,621
What am I supposed to do now?

34
00:02:29,661 --> 00:02:31,531
Do you think I can get through this, Sung Jun?

35
00:02:36,101 --> 00:02:37,871
If only I had gotten my hands on that...

36
00:02:39,671 --> 00:02:40,671
If only...

37
00:02:55,521 --> 00:02:58,321
What do you mean? What's wrong with my dad?

38
00:02:58,521 --> 00:03:02,161
He seemed different at dinner. Something just feels off.

39
00:03:03,931 --> 00:03:06,131
Because I said I could follow you to the US...

40
00:03:06,201 --> 00:03:08,501
without a moment's hesitation, do you think he's upset?

41
00:03:08,831 --> 00:03:11,831
I only said that to show him how strong our bond is.

42
00:03:11,901 --> 00:03:16,071
What? Are you saying you didn't mean it?

43
00:03:16,471 --> 00:03:18,011
Of course I meant it.

44
00:03:19,011 --> 00:03:21,681
I still don't know what decision you'll make,

45
00:03:21,741 --> 00:03:24,151
but we promised we'd never be apart.

46
00:03:25,481 --> 00:03:28,381
If I decide to go back to the US,

47
00:03:29,221 --> 00:03:31,591
will you come with me?

48
00:03:32,461 --> 00:03:33,821
Let me ask you first.

49
00:03:34,621 --> 00:03:38,431
Are you really considering staying here?

50
00:03:39,861 --> 00:03:42,301
I'm considering several options right now.

51
00:03:43,031 --> 00:03:46,441
Let's talk about it again after I've made a firm decision.

52
00:03:47,101 --> 00:03:49,441
It doesn't matter to me where we are.

53
00:03:49,971 --> 00:03:52,781
What's important is that we're together.

54
00:03:53,781 --> 00:03:56,011
You know what I mean, right?

55
00:03:56,611 --> 00:03:57,611
Of course.

56
00:03:58,151 --> 00:04:00,981
And I'm going to Saejuk-dong.

57
00:04:01,181 --> 00:04:03,151
I want to see if there are any roads on the outskirts...

58
00:04:03,151 --> 00:04:05,391
where a car could have crashed. I'm going to see for myself.

59
00:04:05,721 --> 00:04:09,831
I was thinking the same thing. I hoped that if we looked around...

60
00:04:09,891 --> 00:04:11,861
in person, you might remember something.

61
00:04:12,561 --> 00:04:16,001
Okay. I'll work hard all week for the competition.

62
00:04:16,001 --> 00:04:18,871
Will you go with me this weekend?

63
00:04:19,741 --> 00:04:20,971
Yes, I will.

64
00:04:21,541 --> 00:04:23,671
Thank you. All right, shall we start running again?

65
00:04:58,471 --> 00:04:59,541
Well...

66
00:04:59,541 --> 00:05:01,511
I made some rice porridge just in case.

67
00:05:01,511 --> 00:05:02,751
Do you think she can eat any?

68
00:05:03,381 --> 00:05:06,251
Oh, she just barely fell asleep. I'll feed her later.

69
00:05:06,321 --> 00:05:07,751
What are you talking about?

70
00:05:07,821 --> 00:05:10,321
You should go home. You have to work tomorrow.

71
00:05:10,691 --> 00:05:12,721
Leave her to me and go home.

72
00:05:12,961 --> 00:05:14,421
I'll stay and watch her a little longer.

73
00:05:14,721 --> 00:05:18,431
If I go home now, I'll be too worried to sleep anyway.

74
00:05:18,891 --> 00:05:21,461
But is Father not home from work yet?

75
00:05:21,731 --> 00:05:25,571
I know. He's been so busy lately and always comes home late.

76
00:05:27,541 --> 00:05:29,111
- Oh, my. - Honey.

77
00:05:29,441 --> 00:05:33,241
I met him in front of the house, and he was drunk again today.

78
00:05:33,911 --> 00:05:35,611
Oh, what? You are here too?

79
00:05:35,911 --> 00:05:37,011
Why have you been drinking again?

80
00:05:37,351 --> 00:05:39,421
Seriously, why have you been drinking every single day?

81
00:05:39,751 --> 00:05:41,781
Sorry. I did not have that much to drink.

82
00:05:42,621 --> 00:05:44,521
- You're home, Chief Seo? - Oh, General Director Ko.

83
00:05:45,591 --> 00:05:48,091
- What brings you here at this hour? - Why do you think?

84
00:05:48,361 --> 00:05:50,391
He rushed over when he heard Seung Ri was sick,

85
00:05:50,461 --> 00:05:52,331
and he has been taking care of her all day.

86
00:05:52,461 --> 00:05:53,961
What? Is Seung Ri sick?

87
00:05:54,231 --> 00:05:55,531
I mean, what is wrong with her all of a sudden?

88
00:05:55,901 --> 00:05:57,731
You heard Seung Ri was sick this morning,

89
00:05:57,801 --> 00:05:59,571
and you were not even concerned all day?

90
00:06:00,071 --> 00:06:01,201
You did not even call once,

91
00:06:01,271 --> 00:06:03,011
and now you come home drunk at this hour?

92
00:06:03,741 --> 00:06:04,971
Son-in-law Ko has been all day...

93
00:06:06,781 --> 00:06:07,781
I appreciate it.

94
00:06:08,881 --> 00:06:10,151
I am going to head in.

95
00:06:11,111 --> 00:06:12,521
Are you not going to check on Seung Ri?

96
00:06:13,951 --> 00:06:17,921
Goodness, what's gotten into him? He absolutely adores Seung Ri.

97
00:06:18,491 --> 00:06:20,991
Mom, I'm just going to check on her.

98
00:06:21,061 --> 00:06:22,091
Oh, hold on, Seung Woo.

99
00:06:22,391 --> 00:06:23,991
Your sister just managed to fall asleep.

100
00:06:24,061 --> 00:06:25,391
Can you see her tomorrow instead?

101
00:06:26,101 --> 00:06:28,161
It just seems like a cold with a fever,

102
00:06:28,231 --> 00:06:29,531
so do not worry too much.

103
00:06:29,731 --> 00:06:32,401
What? A cold with a fever in this heat?

104
00:06:34,201 --> 00:06:36,341
At least my reliable brother-in-law is here.

105
00:06:36,741 --> 00:06:39,341
Well then, I will turn in. I am not worried anymore.

106
00:06:39,911 --> 00:06:40,911
Hang in there.

107
00:06:42,781 --> 00:06:44,181
You should go get some rest too.

108
00:06:44,611 --> 00:06:46,851
I will stay a little longer and then slip out quietly.

109
00:06:48,951 --> 00:06:50,191
Son-in-law Ko, your devotion...

110
00:06:50,921 --> 00:06:52,421
would move even heaven.

111
00:06:53,021 --> 00:06:54,091
Thank you, really.

112
00:06:55,091 --> 00:06:56,091
Do not mention it.

113
00:06:57,161 --> 00:06:59,401
Thank you for always being so supportive.

114
00:06:59,901 --> 00:07:00,961
The phone has been turned off.

115
00:07:00,961 --> 00:07:03,131
This brat turned his phone off completely.

116
00:07:03,601 --> 00:07:06,171
He is crazy. Completely insane.

117
00:07:06,641 --> 00:07:10,011
I mean, I know he adores Seung Ri, but taking care of her this late?

118
00:07:10,541 --> 00:07:14,841
I raised that boy with kid gloves, my precious, prized son.

119
00:07:14,941 --> 00:07:17,211
It is "prized possession," not "prized son."

120
00:07:17,311 --> 00:07:20,821
Possession, son, whatever. My precious son.

121
00:07:20,821 --> 00:07:21,821
It all means the same thing, right?

122
00:07:23,321 --> 00:07:25,091
Anyway, what is wrong with Seung Ri all of a sudden?

123
00:07:25,151 --> 00:07:27,621
I do not know, and I cannot take it anymore.

124
00:07:27,991 --> 00:07:29,231
I mean, how can they keep someone else's precious son...

125
00:07:29,291 --> 00:07:30,361
there until this hour,

126
00:07:30,431 --> 00:07:31,931
working him like he is a hired nurse?

127
00:07:32,191 --> 00:07:35,701
- I swear... - No, just leave it be.

128
00:07:36,531 --> 00:07:38,931
It is like they say, he is digging his own grave.

129
00:07:39,001 --> 00:07:40,141
He makes his own choices.

130
00:07:40,201 --> 00:07:42,241
It is not like he will listen if we step in.

131
00:07:42,771 --> 00:07:44,041
That ungrateful punk.

132
00:07:45,311 --> 00:07:46,311
Wait a minute, honey.

133
00:07:49,651 --> 00:07:51,451
Oh, my.

134
00:07:52,251 --> 00:07:53,581
Oh my, it is true.

135
00:07:53,921 --> 00:07:56,351
Did you really get into a fight with Chief Seo?

136
00:07:58,621 --> 00:08:00,191
No. It is nothing like that.

137
00:08:01,291 --> 00:08:04,291
I was just coming home after having a drink,

138
00:08:04,361 --> 00:08:08,131
- and I just slammed into the door. - What is this?

139
00:08:08,661 --> 00:08:10,931
Why does it feel like you are avoiding my gaze lately?

140
00:08:12,031 --> 00:08:15,201
I am sure you are hiding something from me.

141
00:08:16,071 --> 00:08:17,871
Come on, what would I be hiding?

142
00:08:18,241 --> 00:08:19,741
Just go to sleep already.

143
00:08:19,811 --> 00:08:21,411
Why would you say I am hiding something?

144
00:08:21,481 --> 00:08:23,111
How can you sleep right now?

145
00:08:23,111 --> 00:08:24,851
I raised our precious Min Ho...

146
00:08:25,181 --> 00:08:26,651
as if he'd blow away or break,

147
00:08:26,881 --> 00:08:28,151
and now we're about to make him...

148
00:08:28,221 --> 00:08:29,251
Chief Seo's son-in-law.

149
00:08:29,321 --> 00:08:32,621
Stop it, really. Stop talking about Chief Seo.

150
00:08:32,691 --> 00:08:33,691
Oh my goodness.

151
00:08:34,421 --> 00:08:36,231
You are going to wake up Father.

152
00:08:36,791 --> 00:08:38,891
Seriously.

153
00:08:39,431 --> 00:08:42,701
Honestly, what gives you the right to get into a fight?

154
00:08:42,771 --> 00:08:44,501
You are crazy. Really.

155
00:08:44,571 --> 00:08:45,771
Hey, stop hitting me.

156
00:09:07,691 --> 00:09:08,691
Min Ho.

157
00:09:11,691 --> 00:09:13,401
Hey, you are awake?

158
00:09:13,961 --> 00:09:15,201
Are you feeling better now?

159
00:09:17,071 --> 00:09:19,201
Have you been here like this all night?

160
00:09:21,471 --> 00:09:23,811
Why? You should've gone home to sleep.

161
00:09:24,371 --> 00:09:26,581
You're so sick. How could I leave?

162
00:09:30,211 --> 00:09:31,881
Well, it seems like your fever's gone down.

163
00:09:32,281 --> 00:09:34,221
Your mother made rice porridge, so eat it,

164
00:09:34,281 --> 00:09:35,851
and we'll go to the hospital together.

165
00:09:37,551 --> 00:09:38,721
Okay, Min Ho.

166
00:09:40,621 --> 00:09:45,191
I'll go with my mom later, so you should hurry and go home.

167
00:09:45,631 --> 00:09:46,761
You have to get to work.

168
00:09:47,261 --> 00:09:48,261
Seung Ri,

169
00:09:48,861 --> 00:09:52,101
no matter what happens to you or who you are,

170
00:09:52,641 --> 00:09:55,401
I'm always on your side. You know that, right?

171
00:09:57,041 --> 00:09:58,141
I know, Min Ho.

172
00:09:59,781 --> 00:10:01,281
I'll call you when I get to work.

173
00:10:01,741 --> 00:10:03,511
Make sure you go to the hospital, okay?

174
00:10:05,281 --> 00:10:06,281
Okay, then.

175
00:11:28,531 --> 00:11:29,531
Oh, my.

176
00:11:30,271 --> 00:11:31,271
Hey, Ko Min Ho.

177
00:11:31,801 --> 00:11:34,541
Did you just pull an all-nighter taking care of Seung Ri?

178
00:11:34,841 --> 00:11:37,411
Yes. I'll get ready for work and be right down.

179
00:11:38,171 --> 00:11:39,171
Stop right there.

180
00:11:40,981 --> 00:11:42,211
Are you really going to be like this?

181
00:11:42,681 --> 00:11:44,211
Are you saying you're going to defy us...

182
00:11:44,281 --> 00:11:45,351
and marry Seung Ri anyway?

183
00:11:46,821 --> 00:11:47,821
Yes.

184
00:11:48,121 --> 00:11:50,621
What? Yes? Did you just say yes?

185
00:11:51,251 --> 00:11:52,521
Have you completely lost your mind?

186
00:11:52,861 --> 00:11:54,761
Did we or did we not tell you Seung Ri is out of the question?

187
00:11:54,821 --> 00:11:56,431
Goodness, Dae Chi.

188
00:11:56,491 --> 00:11:57,961
Why are you raising your voice so early in the morning?

189
00:11:58,861 --> 00:12:01,801
What is all this commotion?

190
00:12:02,331 --> 00:12:04,031
I'm sorry, Father.

191
00:12:04,501 --> 00:12:07,471
Min Ho did something to deserve it, so I was just scolding him, Father.

192
00:12:08,001 --> 00:12:11,411
Min Ho, go on upstairs and get ready for work.

193
00:12:11,711 --> 00:12:13,881
- Yes, Grandfather. - Yes.

194
00:12:15,441 --> 00:12:19,111
But Dae Chi, why are you so against Seung Ri?

195
00:12:20,021 --> 00:12:22,651
The only problem is that Seung Ri won't accept his feelings.

196
00:12:23,051 --> 00:12:26,091
If she did, she would be a flawless daughter-in-law.

197
00:12:27,161 --> 00:12:30,031
Father, Seung Ri is Chief Seo's daughter.

198
00:12:30,091 --> 00:12:31,461
Oh, that's even better.

199
00:12:32,161 --> 00:12:34,731
We've always gotten along like one big family,

200
00:12:35,201 --> 00:12:39,171
and Chief Seo is more loyal and capable at work than anyone.

201
00:12:39,471 --> 00:12:41,071
Wouldn't it be great to have him as an in-law?

202
00:12:42,471 --> 00:12:43,471
Father,

203
00:12:43,871 --> 00:12:45,611
I'm a little hurt to hear you say that.

204
00:12:45,871 --> 00:12:47,811
Our Min Ho is your eldest grandson.

205
00:12:47,811 --> 00:12:49,651
Marrying a secretary's daughter is out of the question.

206
00:12:50,481 --> 00:12:55,151
- The wife of our future head... - That's enough.

207
00:12:56,551 --> 00:13:00,221
Well, breakfast is ready, so everyone, come inside.

208
00:13:00,521 --> 00:13:01,561
You too, Secretary Ju.

209
00:13:01,921 --> 00:13:05,391
Oh no, it's quite all right. I'll eat in the annex.

210
00:13:06,761 --> 00:13:07,761
Yes.

211
00:13:09,361 --> 00:13:10,501
My goodness.

212
00:13:10,871 --> 00:13:14,871
Father is being so unreasonable. Why is he always like that with us?

213
00:13:14,941 --> 00:13:17,241
It is always "Enough!" or a tsk...

214
00:13:17,311 --> 00:13:19,611
and a glare that cuts through us.

215
00:13:19,681 --> 00:13:21,241
Then maybe you should stop doing things...

216
00:13:21,311 --> 00:13:24,851
that make him say "That's enough" or tsk his tongue at you.

217
00:13:24,911 --> 00:13:27,821
Oh, what's this? Starting in on me first thing in the morning?

218
00:13:28,351 --> 00:13:31,121
Could you please just mind your own business?

219
00:13:31,451 --> 00:13:33,961
Hey, Yong Man. Can I have a word with you?

220
00:13:34,491 --> 00:13:37,031
Sure, go ahead. I'm all ears.

221
00:13:38,991 --> 00:13:41,701
Look, I didn't want to have to say this.

222
00:13:42,831 --> 00:13:44,631
But let's keep some boundaries, okay?

223
00:13:45,171 --> 00:13:47,341
- You're just our family's... - Wait!

224
00:13:47,771 --> 00:13:49,071
I just remembered something.

225
00:13:49,911 --> 00:13:51,771
About 25 years ago,

226
00:13:52,511 --> 00:13:53,941
why did Gwon Sik and Sung Jun...

227
00:13:54,011 --> 00:13:55,911
suddenly come looking for President Ko?

228
00:13:56,811 --> 00:13:58,881
What?

229
00:13:59,311 --> 00:14:01,221
That was around the time you were promoted...

230
00:14:01,281 --> 00:14:02,581
to executive director, right?

231
00:14:03,591 --> 00:14:05,921
I was heading to your office...

232
00:14:05,991 --> 00:14:07,461
on the Chairman's orders...

233
00:14:07,861 --> 00:14:12,731
when the door flew open. You ran out,

234
00:14:12,901 --> 00:14:14,261
and right behind you,

235
00:14:14,331 --> 00:14:16,971
Sung Jun and Gwon Sik rushed out...

236
00:14:17,031 --> 00:14:20,201
This is unbelievable. We were talking.

237
00:14:20,271 --> 00:14:21,971
Why are you suddenly changing the subject?

238
00:14:22,271 --> 00:14:24,371
- Hey, come on. Come here. - Okay.

239
00:14:24,441 --> 00:14:26,581
Father is waiting, so let's go inside. Come on, move.

240
00:14:26,581 --> 00:14:28,211
Gosh, seriously.

241
00:14:30,481 --> 00:14:32,051
What could it be?

242
00:14:32,411 --> 00:14:36,851
The reason President Ko shrinks whenever that story comes up.

243
00:14:39,621 --> 00:14:41,721
Manager Seo Seung Ri called in sick today...

244
00:14:41,791 --> 00:14:44,531
because she's not feeling well, so please be aware of that.

245
00:14:44,831 --> 00:14:48,331
What? Again today? Is she that unwell?

246
00:14:48,701 --> 00:14:50,901
It seems like she has a really bad flu.

247
00:14:52,171 --> 00:14:54,241
Manager Seo has never taken a single sick day...

248
00:14:54,301 --> 00:14:55,641
since I started working here.

249
00:14:56,001 --> 00:14:58,411
We'll proceed with today's meeting without Manager Seo,

250
00:14:58,471 --> 00:14:59,471
so we'll gather in the conference room...

251
00:14:59,471 --> 00:15:01,311
- in 30 minutes. - Okay.

252
00:15:07,051 --> 00:15:08,481
The phone is currently switched off.

253
00:15:08,551 --> 00:15:10,251
Please leave your message after the beep...

254
00:15:17,391 --> 00:15:18,461
How's Manager Seo?

255
00:15:20,031 --> 00:15:21,031
She's very sick.

256
00:15:22,931 --> 00:15:23,931
She's on sick leave and has been in bed...

257
00:15:24,001 --> 00:15:25,001
for two days straight.

258
00:15:25,131 --> 00:15:27,841
She must have been incredibly shocked.

259
00:15:28,571 --> 00:15:30,371
There's nothing I can do.

260
00:15:31,311 --> 00:15:32,871
I can't even make an excuse.

261
00:15:37,611 --> 00:15:38,611
Gwon Sik.

262
00:15:39,921 --> 00:15:42,991
If that thing still exists,

263
00:15:44,091 --> 00:15:45,791
what do you think you could do with it?

264
00:15:46,991 --> 00:15:48,291
What do you mean?

265
00:15:49,421 --> 00:15:52,731
Don't you think there could be an even bigger fallout?

266
00:15:53,661 --> 00:15:54,701
Do you, by any chance,

267
00:15:55,201 --> 00:15:56,231
have it?

268
00:15:56,971 --> 00:15:57,971
You do?

269
00:15:58,601 --> 00:16:00,241
That's not what I meant.

270
00:16:01,501 --> 00:16:04,911
If the whole truth comes out, do you really think Manager Seo...

271
00:16:04,971 --> 00:16:06,681
will be more at ease than she is now?

272
00:16:07,611 --> 00:16:09,411
And Team Leader Ko, the main victim,

273
00:16:10,211 --> 00:16:12,381
could suffer even greater harm.

274
00:16:22,991 --> 00:16:24,731
Chief Seo, do you have a moment?

275
00:16:25,261 --> 00:16:27,331
Oh, why?

276
00:16:27,901 --> 00:16:30,571
Yes. Yes, I understand.

277
00:16:31,871 --> 00:16:34,071
You two carry on. I've been summoned.

278
00:16:34,371 --> 00:16:35,941
- Yes. - Okay.

279
00:16:37,841 --> 00:16:39,141
I heard Seung Ri is sick.

280
00:16:40,111 --> 00:16:42,241
Well...

281
00:16:42,711 --> 00:16:44,011
I think it's the flu.

282
00:16:44,381 --> 00:16:47,681
The flu? She seemed fine just a few days ago...

283
00:16:47,751 --> 00:16:50,091
when she was drinking with the General Director.

284
00:16:50,891 --> 00:16:53,121
I'll stop by your place after work today.

285
00:16:53,291 --> 00:16:55,491
Oh, no. There's no need for that.

286
00:16:55,821 --> 00:16:56,831
What?

287
00:16:57,161 --> 00:17:00,601
Seung Ri hates people seeing her when she's sick.

288
00:17:00,861 --> 00:17:02,031
You know how she is.

289
00:17:03,031 --> 00:17:06,301
But I'll be sure to tell her you wanted to visit.

290
00:17:06,901 --> 00:17:08,301
You don't have to go through the trouble.

291
00:17:09,171 --> 00:17:12,611
Yes, I understand. I'll excuse myself then.

292
00:17:24,991 --> 00:17:27,361
It's me. How's Seung Ri?

293
00:17:29,461 --> 00:17:31,831
Well, she managed to eat a little rice porridge...

294
00:17:31,891 --> 00:17:33,101
and fell back asleep.

295
00:17:33,701 --> 00:17:35,601
I offered to go to the hospital with her,

296
00:17:35,601 --> 00:17:38,531
but she said she'll go by herself after a nap.

297
00:17:38,831 --> 00:17:40,741
Okay, keep a close eye on her...

298
00:17:41,401 --> 00:17:42,701
and let me know if anything happens.

299
00:17:44,071 --> 00:17:46,141
(President Ko Dae Chi)

300
00:17:46,781 --> 00:17:47,881
What's Chief Seo up to?

301
00:17:48,211 --> 00:17:50,781
Team Leader Ko is there, so they're talking right now.

302
00:17:51,151 --> 00:17:53,181
Team Leader Ko?

303
00:17:54,281 --> 00:17:55,281
Where are you going?

304
00:17:56,591 --> 00:17:59,591
Are you worried about what they're talking about?

305
00:18:01,191 --> 00:18:02,191
What did you say?

306
00:18:02,621 --> 00:18:03,931
You know very well...

307
00:18:03,991 --> 00:18:07,361
that Team Leader Ko is looking into the past accident.

308
00:18:10,771 --> 00:18:12,431
Manager Seo has found out everything.

309
00:18:13,271 --> 00:18:15,101
Of course, it's only half the truth.

310
00:18:15,641 --> 00:18:17,841
What do you mean?

311
00:18:18,371 --> 00:18:19,641
You mean Manager Seo found out everything?

312
00:18:20,211 --> 00:18:23,481
That her father was imprisoned...

313
00:18:23,881 --> 00:18:25,451
for causing Gyeol's father's crash.

314
00:18:26,111 --> 00:18:27,981
What?

315
00:18:29,251 --> 00:18:31,021
Chief Seo is having a very hard time right now.

316
00:18:31,991 --> 00:18:33,021
Leave him alone.

317
00:18:34,591 --> 00:18:37,491
What does that mean?

318
00:18:37,891 --> 00:18:39,561
What on earth do you mean by that?

319
00:18:52,771 --> 00:18:54,241
Eun Nim, follow my lead.

320
00:19:13,331 --> 00:19:14,431
Careful.

321
00:19:17,571 --> 00:19:21,041
- What are you doing this early? - What does it look like I'm doing?

322
00:19:21,701 --> 00:19:24,211
I was stretching before starting work.

323
00:19:24,671 --> 00:19:25,671
Stretching?

324
00:19:27,111 --> 00:19:29,281
Oh, stretching.

325
00:19:29,781 --> 00:19:33,681
- Should we stretch together, then? - Together?

326
00:19:34,321 --> 00:19:35,321
One moment.

327
00:19:36,951 --> 00:19:38,151
Let's see.

328
00:19:53,441 --> 00:19:54,441
Done.

329
00:19:55,041 --> 00:19:57,471
That's enough stretching.

330
00:20:08,981 --> 00:20:10,291
What do you think you are doing?

331
00:20:11,451 --> 00:20:12,691
What? It's just...

332
00:20:13,621 --> 00:20:16,221
We're close enough to share a little kiss.

333
00:20:16,291 --> 00:20:18,831
Close enough? What do you mean by that?

334
00:20:19,291 --> 00:20:21,261
Well, back then, in front of your mother,

335
00:20:21,561 --> 00:20:23,371
you confessed that you liked me.

336
00:20:24,431 --> 00:20:25,431
I...

337
00:20:25,831 --> 00:20:27,001
I like Bung Woo.

338
00:20:27,971 --> 00:20:28,971
What?

339
00:20:29,941 --> 00:20:32,741
- What did you say? - Because he's the man I like.

340
00:20:33,281 --> 00:20:35,481
So, please just stop it.

341
00:20:36,881 --> 00:20:40,381
And I already confessed that I liked you, Bung Nim.

342
00:20:40,451 --> 00:20:42,681
So weren't we dating?

343
00:20:43,521 --> 00:20:47,561
That was just because my mom was hitting you so hard.

344
00:20:48,661 --> 00:20:50,431
And violence is wrong.

345
00:20:50,961 --> 00:20:53,301
It was a humanitarian gesture.

346
00:20:53,701 --> 00:20:55,461
A humanitarian gesture?

347
00:20:56,701 --> 00:20:58,231
A humanitarian gesture?

348
00:20:58,771 --> 00:21:00,041
Is that really true?

349
00:21:01,401 --> 00:21:02,401
Unbelievable.

350
00:21:03,411 --> 00:21:06,211
Seriously, where is it? Grandma.

351
00:21:06,811 --> 00:21:07,841
Grandma!

352
00:21:08,581 --> 00:21:10,881
Goodness, why do you keep calling me?

353
00:21:10,951 --> 00:21:13,621
Goodness, I was just trying to nap.

354
00:21:13,681 --> 00:21:16,991
- Where are the flowers? - The flowers? I threw them out.

355
00:21:17,251 --> 00:21:21,791
- You threw them out? Why? - They were all wilted.

356
00:21:21,861 --> 00:21:25,231
Seriously? Where did you throw them?

357
00:21:25,291 --> 00:21:26,291
Where do you think?

358
00:21:26,361 --> 00:21:28,661
I put them in a trash bag and took it outside.

359
00:21:28,731 --> 00:21:31,231
Seriously, you didn't even tell me.

360
00:21:32,131 --> 00:21:33,131
Seriously.

361
00:21:33,201 --> 00:21:34,941
(Grandma Pancake)

362
00:21:35,001 --> 00:21:36,741
Oh no, where is it?

363
00:21:39,071 --> 00:21:42,211
- Aunt Cho Rong, what are you doing? - Hey, Bit Na.

364
00:21:42,481 --> 00:21:45,081
- I'm just looking for something. - What are you looking for...

365
00:21:45,151 --> 00:21:46,721
that has you digging through trash bags?

366
00:21:47,281 --> 00:21:48,921
It seems important. Do you want me to help?

367
00:21:48,981 --> 00:21:51,091
No, it's okay. You should get going.

368
00:21:51,151 --> 00:21:53,191
I think it's almost time for your class.

369
00:21:53,591 --> 00:21:55,791
Okay, then. Let's go.

370
00:21:55,861 --> 00:21:57,061
(Our Happy Days Real Estate)

371
00:21:58,791 --> 00:21:59,791
Found it.

372
00:22:01,531 --> 00:22:03,301
Put that back.

373
00:22:03,901 --> 00:22:07,071
Why are you pulling out those wilted flowers?

374
00:22:07,341 --> 00:22:10,941
I was going to dry them and make dried flowers.

375
00:22:11,011 --> 00:22:12,011
(Our Happy Days Real Estate)

376
00:22:13,211 --> 00:22:15,541
Cho Rong, that flower...

377
00:22:15,911 --> 00:22:17,311
Isn't that the one I gave you?

378
00:22:18,211 --> 00:22:21,681
Yes. It was so pretty that I wanted to dry it.

379
00:22:23,251 --> 00:22:26,051
Good grief. That girl...

380
00:22:26,421 --> 00:22:27,421
Excuse me, ma'am.

381
00:22:28,021 --> 00:22:30,461
I'm sorry, but do you happen to know where my mother went?

382
00:22:30,531 --> 00:22:32,761
Your mom? She went to the market a while ago.

383
00:22:33,131 --> 00:22:35,001
I heard she's inviting the Chairman...

384
00:22:35,061 --> 00:22:37,301
and his wife over to your house tomorrow.

385
00:22:37,831 --> 00:22:38,831
Yes.

386
00:22:39,701 --> 00:22:41,501
- Thank you. - Right.

387
00:22:42,771 --> 00:22:45,311
He's a nice man,

388
00:22:45,841 --> 00:22:47,581
but he's a single dad.

389
00:22:48,041 --> 00:22:49,041
Sun Bun.

390
00:22:50,451 --> 00:22:51,811
What did you just say?

391
00:22:52,351 --> 00:22:55,921
- Me? I didn't say anything. - You just did.

392
00:22:55,981 --> 00:22:58,151
You called my Eun Hyung a single dad.

393
00:22:58,321 --> 00:23:00,721
Well, you know, it's just that...

394
00:23:01,561 --> 00:23:05,091
- It's the truth, isn't it? - How is that the truth?

395
00:23:05,091 --> 00:23:06,661
They're still in the cooling-off period.

396
00:23:06,731 --> 00:23:10,501
That means my Eun Hyung can still get back together with her.

397
00:23:11,031 --> 00:23:13,641
Don't you dare call him a single dad again.

398
00:23:13,941 --> 00:23:15,041
Do you understand?

399
00:23:17,671 --> 00:23:21,611
Then they should hurry up and get back together. Good grief.

400
00:23:27,851 --> 00:23:30,751
Why does she keep harping on about him being a single dad? Honestly.

401
00:23:32,491 --> 00:23:34,061
Grandma.

402
00:23:34,991 --> 00:23:35,991
- You're back, Mother? - Yes.

403
00:23:36,061 --> 00:23:39,031
Bit Na, did you have a good day at preschool?

404
00:23:39,491 --> 00:23:41,261
Yes, I just got home.

405
00:23:41,961 --> 00:23:43,731
I heard you invited the Chairman and Grandma over tomorrow.

406
00:23:43,831 --> 00:23:45,971
I wanted to cook a meal for them myself.

407
00:23:46,101 --> 00:23:47,271
That's a great idea.

408
00:23:47,401 --> 00:23:50,871
Are Great-Grandma and Great-Grandpa coming to our house tomorrow?

409
00:23:51,271 --> 00:23:54,581
- I can't wait. - Wash your hands. I'll get a snack.

410
00:23:54,641 --> 00:23:55,741
Okay, Grandma.

411
00:23:58,151 --> 00:23:59,151
You.

412
00:23:59,581 --> 00:24:01,421
Did you meet with Ji Seon? Did your talk go well?

413
00:24:01,881 --> 00:24:02,981
What talk?

414
00:24:03,321 --> 00:24:05,191
About getting back together.

415
00:24:05,691 --> 00:24:06,691
Oh, that.

416
00:24:07,091 --> 00:24:09,221
I can't be the one to suggest we get back together.

417
00:24:09,291 --> 00:24:11,531
You have to convince her for Bit Na's sake.

418
00:24:11,591 --> 00:24:12,961
What are you talking about?

419
00:24:13,061 --> 00:24:15,461
I put her through so much because of my money problems.

420
00:24:16,201 --> 00:24:18,431
I just want to let her live her own life for a bit.

421
00:24:19,301 --> 00:24:21,001
And there's no guarantee things won't be...

422
00:24:21,071 --> 00:24:22,501
the same if we get back together.

423
00:24:22,571 --> 00:24:24,671
What about Bit Na? What happens to her?

424
00:24:24,911 --> 00:24:28,281
Bit Na has been talking to and seeing Ji Seon regularly,

425
00:24:28,681 --> 00:24:30,381
so she's become a lot more emotionally stable.

426
00:24:30,611 --> 00:24:33,181
Who says she's stable?

427
00:24:33,181 --> 00:24:35,021
She only seems that way on the surface.

428
00:24:35,451 --> 00:24:38,251
Do you have any idea how much this has scarred her?

429
00:24:38,491 --> 00:24:40,521
Anyway, I'm going to let Ji Seon decide.

430
00:24:41,161 --> 00:24:42,291
I'm heading to my class now.

431
00:24:46,661 --> 00:24:48,361
He's so frustrating. Seriously.

432
00:24:56,741 --> 00:24:57,811
Yes, it's me.

433
00:24:58,541 --> 00:24:59,571
Why?

434
00:25:00,641 --> 00:25:03,381
It would be easier for you if I brought something.

435
00:25:05,351 --> 00:25:07,721
Okay, fine. I'll come empty-handed.

436
00:25:09,151 --> 00:25:10,891
All right. See you tomorrow.

437
00:25:12,191 --> 00:25:14,521
Did Yeon Soon tell you not to bring anything tomorrow?

438
00:25:14,791 --> 00:25:15,791
Yes.

439
00:25:16,521 --> 00:25:18,461
I was thinking of at least making some kimchi,

440
00:25:19,291 --> 00:25:21,601
but she said she'd handle everything and told us to come empty-handed.

441
00:25:22,501 --> 00:25:25,271
She's just trying to save you the trouble.

442
00:25:25,571 --> 00:25:28,501
I'm more worried about making my daughter do all the work.

443
00:25:29,841 --> 00:25:30,971
Young Hwa,

444
00:25:31,511 --> 00:25:34,511
was there something you'd always wanted to do with your daughter?

445
00:25:35,311 --> 00:25:36,741
Something I've wanted to do?

446
00:25:38,251 --> 00:25:41,481
- There are so many things. - What do you want most?

447
00:25:44,391 --> 00:25:46,421
Sleep beside her for a night.

448
00:25:47,761 --> 00:25:52,091
I can still picture her as a child...

449
00:25:52,861 --> 00:25:54,301
asleep in my arms to my lullaby.

450
00:25:55,401 --> 00:25:57,331
That's what I want to do the most.

451
00:25:58,431 --> 00:25:59,771
Then you should do it tomorrow.

452
00:26:00,131 --> 00:26:03,301
Oh, come on. How could I do that in a house full of people?

453
00:26:03,741 --> 00:26:07,411
- I was just saying. - What's the big deal?

454
00:26:08,241 --> 00:26:09,341
Or...

455
00:26:09,811 --> 00:26:12,411
you two could take a trip together.

456
00:26:12,751 --> 00:26:15,121
How could I go on a trip and leave you behind?

457
00:26:15,221 --> 00:26:18,221
What, are you worried I can't manage one night by myself?

458
00:26:18,291 --> 00:26:19,421
Oh, please. It's fine.

459
00:26:20,121 --> 00:26:22,791
Being able to see her like this...

460
00:26:22,791 --> 00:26:24,061
whenever I get a chance is enough for me.

461
00:26:27,131 --> 00:26:29,201
(Saejuk-dong Development Zone)

462
00:26:34,571 --> 00:26:36,571
- What are you doing? - Oh, this?

463
00:26:36,701 --> 00:26:39,011
I'm looking at the satellite map.

464
00:26:39,341 --> 00:26:42,441
Saejuk-dong is completely different than it was 25 years ago.

465
00:26:43,381 --> 00:26:45,551
I'm comparing it with the old maps,

466
00:26:46,151 --> 00:26:48,081
but it's changed so much that you can't find a trace of its past.

467
00:26:48,081 --> 00:26:50,551
The whole area is covered in buildings and apartments.

468
00:26:51,791 --> 00:26:54,521
All this work just to help your boyfriend recover his memory.

469
00:26:55,261 --> 00:26:58,531
- Should we call it a day, kiddo? - Okay.

470
00:26:59,131 --> 00:27:02,561
By the way, Manager Seo seems really sick.

471
00:27:02,661 --> 00:27:04,571
Don't you think we should visit her?

472
00:27:05,601 --> 00:27:08,771
I already asked Chief Seo, and he said...

473
00:27:08,841 --> 00:27:10,871
she doesn't want anyone to see her when she's sick.

474
00:27:11,841 --> 00:27:13,011
I guess that makes sense.

475
00:27:14,511 --> 00:27:16,611
I hope she feels a bit better by tomorrow.

476
00:27:17,151 --> 00:27:19,381
- Okay, let's get going. - Okay.

477
00:27:21,551 --> 00:27:23,851
(General Director's Office)

478
00:27:23,921 --> 00:27:27,521
- Are you leaving, General Director? - Yes. You two are here late.

479
00:27:27,591 --> 00:27:28,621
Right.

480
00:27:29,491 --> 00:27:30,491
Just a moment.

481
00:27:32,661 --> 00:27:33,661
Yes, Mother.

482
00:27:34,901 --> 00:27:37,271
What? Seung Ri? Since when?

483
00:27:37,271 --> 00:27:39,371
She said she'd go to the hospital over five hours ago,

484
00:27:39,431 --> 00:27:40,501
and she's not answering her phone.

485
00:27:41,371 --> 00:27:42,841
What am I going to do?

486
00:27:43,601 --> 00:27:45,411
Where on earth could she have gone?

487
00:27:45,941 --> 00:27:47,881
What is it? Did something happen to Seung Ri?

488
00:27:49,081 --> 00:27:51,111
Mother, I'm heading over there right now.

489
00:27:51,651 --> 00:27:52,651
Yes.

490
00:28:01,161 --> 00:28:03,791
(Our Happy Days)

491
00:28:03,991 --> 00:28:07,531
- They say our Seung Ri disappeared. - What? Seo Seung Ri disappeared?

492
00:28:07,631 --> 00:28:10,471
I have nowhere left to go now.

493
00:28:10,931 --> 00:28:14,971
- My whole world has collapsed. - How can I call myself a father?

494
00:28:15,601 --> 00:28:18,141
- Am I even human? - You said it yourself.

495
00:28:18,141 --> 00:28:20,311
That you were the one who brought Gwon Sik to me.

496
00:28:20,381 --> 00:28:23,281
- Then you should feel guilty too. - What's that supposed to mean?

497
00:28:23,341 --> 00:28:24,351
Hey, you.

498
00:28:29,781 --> 00:28:32,521
(Our Happy Days)
